    common={'time':stamp(),'review_kind':'PRIMARY research only','original_JPG_and_formal_native_PNG_actually_viewed':True,'fresh_noop_pass':True,'independent_review_performed':False,'controls_required_as_hard_gate':False,'mark_count_cap_imposed':False,'full_old_raw_read':True,'global_call_scan':str(HERE/'global_old_call_and_objection_scan_v2.json')}
    proof={'question_id':'Solid212',**common,'formal_answer':'C','unique_value':240,'proof':'Unroll the cylindrical wall using horizontal arclength s modulo circumference30*pi and vertical coordinate z in[0,80]. At each z the ribbon occupies one total horizontal arclength interval of width3, possibly split at the seam. The surface area element is ds dz, so area=integral_0^80 3 dz=240. The two total turns determine slope, not a second multiplicity in the area. Seam wrapping preserves total width. All options are distinct; C alone is240. No min/max optimization is requested.','source_native_caveat':'Native analytic model explicitly treats the overall ribbon angular extent as4*pi; nonzero width means both printed A/B endpoint incidences cannot also force each boundary separately to make exactly2 turns. Area remains240 without assuming either boundary has exactly2 turns. Width3 is intrinsic horizontal surface arclength, not the projected chord or normal width. Source calls the stripe red, but actual JPG/formal retain white interior and black bounds; do not invent red face paint.','considered_hypotheses':[{'idea':'One complete turn unit as whole ribbon, preset120','objection':'The native visible stripe consists of disconnected visible pieces; a full turn runs behind the silo. Existing black silhouettes are view-dependent tangency loci, not a physical unit boundary. Completing a colored turn or cross-level bracket would add a new partition/range that is not shown. Two front pieces are not one complete turn.'},{'idea':'Horizontal width3 as normal slanted width','objection':'A new perpendicular-width marker would imply a false measurement range; coloring only existing bounds gives no targeted transfer of the horizontal dimension. It would be arbitrary stripe emphasis.'},{'idea':'Two80-foot revolutions, preset480','objection':'Repeats the prior rejected full-height/whole-stripe hypothesis, with no new auditable partial-range information. Cosmetic changes cannot repair it.'}],'decision':'reasoned_skip_no_clean_materially_new_human_unambiguous_design','new_markers':[],'new_candidate_frozen':False,'new_API_calls':0,'old_calls_observed':0}
    save(HERE/'Solid212/primary_math_native_and_skip.json',proof)
    front={(x,y,z) for x,y,z in product(range(3),repeat=3) if y in (0,2) and ((x,z) in ((0,0),(0,2),(2,0),(2,2),(1,1)))}
    sides={(x,y,z) for x,y,z in product(range(3),repeat=3) if x in (0,2) and ((y,z) in ((0,1),(1,0),(1,2),(2,1)))}
    caps={(1,1,0),(1,1,2)}
    shaded=front|sides|caps
    assert (len(front),len(sides),len(caps),len(shaded))==(10,8,2,20)
    assert not front&sides and not front&caps and not sides&caps
    unshaded=set(product(range(3),repeat=3))-shaded
    proof={'question_id':'Solid222',**common,'formal_answer':'20','unique_value':20,'proof':'Use small-cube identities(x,y,z) in{0,1,2}^3. Front/back y=0,2 shade four corners plus face center:10 distinct cubes. Left/right x=0,2 shade four edge-middle face cells:8 distinct cubes. Top/bottom z=0,2 shade only the face center:2 distinct cubes. These sets are pairwise disjoint, so their union has20 members. The seven remaining cubes are explicitly listed. Opposite-face patterns are symmetric within each face, so no orientation ambiguity changes this union. No minimum/maximum is requested; the count is fixed.','painted_front_back':sorted(front),'painted_left_right':sorted(sides),'painted_top_bottom':sorted(caps),'all_27_cubes':list(product(range(3),repeat=3)),'all_shaded_cube_identities':sorted(shaded),'all_unshaded_cube_identities':sorted(unshaded),'considered_hypotheses':[{'idea':'Duplicate every visible painted face count to represent opposite faces','objection':'It gives2*(5+4+1)=20 exactly because there are no painted incidences overlapping on one cube. It is not a wrong counting hypothesis.'},{'idea':'Copy front checkerboard corner/center class to top/right, targeting14','objection':'No true receiver correspondence makes the actual right-face edge-middle cells into front corner cells. Marking white receiver cells as shaded would change the target; marking only the old two staggered corners repeats the18 design. The old14 final cannot be retroactively adopted.'},{'idea':'Group symmetry classes rather than cube identities','objection':'Merely marking representative centers/corners gives no human-clear correspondence telling class count from actual multiplicity. A coloring-only variant would be decoration or repeat the old pattern confusion, not a substantive targeted new geometric design.'}],'old_preset':'18','old_full_finals':['26','14'],'old_pair_status':'miss','decision':'reasoned_skip_no_clean_materially_new_human_unambiguous_design','new_markers':[],'new_candidate_frozen':False,'new_API_calls':0}
    save(HERE/'Solid222/primary_math_native_and_skip.json',proof)
    dims={'given':(10,5),'A':(20,5),'B':(10,10),'C':(5,10),'D':(20,10)}
    vols={k:r*r*h for k,(r,h) in dims.items()}
    ratios={k:str(F(v,vols['given'])) for k,v in vols.items() if k!='given'}
    assert [k for k in ratios if F(ratios[k])==2]==['B']
    save(HERE/'Solid227/primary_math_native.json',{'question_id':'Solid227',**common,'formal_answer':'B','unique_answer':'B','radius_height_pairs':dims,'volume_coefficients_of_pi':vols,'ratios_to_given':ratios,'proof':'The shown top-face line is center-to-rim in both actual JPG and native scene; it is a radius. V=pi*r^2*h gives500pi for the given, then2000pi,1000pi,250pi,4000pi forA-D. ExactlyB is1000pi=2*500pi. C has half the given volume. No min/max condition is requested.','native_dimension_correction':'An early commentary in this unit incorrectly called the horizontal label a diameter before full native review. That statement was corrected before any design/test. The old design correctly says radius; an old model response and prospective brief contain diameter confusion. They remain immutable. All new math and design use actual radii.','old_preset':'A','old_complete_finals':['E','B'],'old_pair_status':'miss','new_direction':'Cross-role given radius10 toC height10 and given height5 toC radius5. A precisely declared inverse-volume comparison would uniquely selectC; the requested forward comparison still uniquely givesB. The matching numeric values are already printed, not new equality stipulations.'})
    heights={'A':F(1,2),'B':F(1,3),'C':F(1,17)}
    heights['D']=1-sum(heights.values())
    order=['C','B','A','D']
    separate=sum(2+4*h for h in heights.values())
    contact=[min(heights[a],heights[b]) for a,b in zip(order,order[1:])]
    steps=[abs(heights[a]-heights[b]) for a,b in zip(order,order[1:])]
    transverse=heights['C']+sum(steps)+heights['D']
    area=separate-2*sum(contact)
    assert heights['D']==F(11,102) and separate==12 and sum(contact)==F(1,2) and transverse==1 and area==11
    save(HERE/'Solid235/primary_math_native.json',{'question_id':'Solid235',**common,'formal_answer':'E','unique_value':11,'heights':{k:str(v) for k,v in heights.items()},'output_order':order,'contacts':list(map(str,contact)),'separate_area':str(separate),'exposed_step_heights':list(map(str,steps)),'transverse_area_ends_plus_risers':str(transverse),'proof':'The one-cubic-foot cube has side1. SlabsA,B,C,D have heights1/2,1/3,1/17,11/102. The displayed common-bottom orderC-B-A-D has only three unit-depth side contacts of areas1/17,1/3,11/102; they sum1/2. Separate surface areas sum(2+4h)=12. Remove each contact twice:12-2*(1/2)=11, uniquelyE. Independently, four exposed unit tops plus four exposed unit bottoms contribute8; the two long vertical sides contribute2*sum(h)=2; outer ends and step risers totalhC+|hB-hC|+|hA-hB|+|hD-hA|+hD=2hA=1. Total8+2+1=11. No minimum/maximum is requested.','native_details':'Lower scene drawing coordinates round a few visible horizontal traces to8 decimals while rational heights are recoverable from formal conditions and original solid_models. No pixel lengths are used as mathematical givens. D is partly occluded by A; its existing visible rear and right top edges still bound a unit top face.','old_preset':'A','old_complete_finals':['11 (E)','6 (A)'],'old_pair_status':'miss','old_raw_caveat':'Run1 final11 follows many inconsistent intermediate answers and incorrectD=5/34. Only terminal11 is the final; it is not proof-quality reasoning. Run2 final6 matchesA once.','new_direction':'Match the original unit top-face corner to the actual unit top-face corners on all four output slabs. Hypothesis: transfer one exposed top per slab into a one-sided surface inventory, omitting all four exposed bottom faces;4 top+3 vertical=7, presetB. This is a separate omission error from the old false full-unit contact-area subtraction.'})
    helpers=[TASK/'delivery_bridge_adapter.py',TASK/'runtime_isolation.py',TASK/'harness/quicktest3_isolated.py']+[PROJECT/'SolidGeometry/workbench'/s for s in ('mathvision_plugins.py','render_plugins.py','renderer_adapter.py','partial_style.py','workbench_io.py','plugin.schema.json','quick_test.py','config.json')]+[PROJECT/'dataset_tools/mathvision_workbench.py']
